All contracts, the prover and the web app were written for Talyx during the Portaldot Hacker House 2026
(14 October to 6 November 2026). Third-party code and data it relies on:

Contracts (contracts/)
  forge-std (git submodule, commit dc647cc030d9d65910d8f1172a0cde48d7106e32)
    https://github.com/foundry-rs/forge-std, MIT / Apache-2.0. Tests only.
  blake2b-solidity, https://github.com/dhl/blake2b-solidity, MIT.
    Not copied. src/lib/Blake2b.sol is written for Talyx and follows the same approach: BLAKE2b driven through the
    EIP-152 F precompile.
  solidity-merkle-trees (PolkadotTrie), https://github.com/polytope-labs/solidity-merkle-trees, Apache-2.0.
    Not copied. src/lib/Trie.sol is written for Talyx and walks the same Substrate trie node format, with
    blake2b-256 node hashes and layout V1.
  BridgeZero, https://github.com/jonathan-moore58/bridge-zero, Apache-2.0.
    Read as a reference for how Revive contract storage sits in a child trie. No code is used.

Prover (prover/)
  @polkadot/api 17.0.2, @polkadot/util 14.0.3, @polkadot/util-crypto 14.0.3 (Apache-2.0)
  viem 2.57.14 (MIT)
  tsx, typescript (MIT / Apache-2.0), development only

Web (web/)
